{
  "requirement": "Configure the domain’s project files with {cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_sources`. `Domain::project_sources` binds those files to the domain for Rust searches and agent inspection. Each hit identifies a node under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** I derived three from `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.attachment`:\n1. Project files configured with `with_sources` are bound to the domain by `Domain::project_sources`.\n2. The bound files serve searches and agent inspection.\n3. Each hit identifies a node under `source_nodes`.\n\n**Attachment and binding.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` builds a domain with `ValidationCache::with_agent(config).with_sources(Sources::new(dir))`.\n- It asserts that the agent's tool list gains `list_sources`, `outline_source`, `search_text`, `search_structure` and `finish_search`.\n- The agent actually uses the bound files. `list_sources` returns numeric node ids, and `read_node` of a listed file returns the mapped snapshot text. `search_text` returns three matches for `^excerpt `.\n- The binding is scoped to the supplied project directory. The test sets up an ignored file and a `visible-old` sibling and checks which paths reach the domain's `source_node` mapping.\n- The test repeats this for two independent executions.\n\n**No sources configured.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled]` asserts `project_sources()` is `None` when no sources are attached.\n- `configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` has no sources attached. It asserts that the tool list is exactly the four base tools, so the source tools are absent.\n\n**Hits identify nodes.**\n- In the configured-agent test, each search match carries a `node` and a `tag`. `read_node` on a hit's node works.\n- The recorded dependencies are asserted exactly. They include `TestNode` ids 8 and 9, which map to the alpha and beta files with fingerprints built by `OutlineContent::from_source(...).at_offset(0)`. This shows that search hits resolve to graph nodes through the domain's `source_node` mapping.\n- The `visible/selected.txt` assertion shows the file was routed through the domain's mapping with the expected `OutlineData`.\n\n**Residual risk.** `search_structure` appears in the tool list but is not exercised in these tests. The requirement's attachment obligation is the binding and the node identity of hits. `search_text` exercises both, and structure-search behavior belongs to separate search requirements. This is not a gap for the subject. No unacknowledged gap remains.",
  "references": "6c8ce8157893ac62f7994d2ab6e8b2ce8aea5bbb38571d10c5ffa8d4eb885fad",
